  "report_period": "Week 26 (20th Jun to 27th Jun 2025)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Mitsubishi Ore Transport have committed the Kamsarmax \"Santa Graciela\" 82/2013 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 03/2028, DD 03/2026) to Singaporean interests at high USD 18 mill. Remind you that back in March, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Energy Hope\" 82/2012 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 02/2027) was sold at USD 17 mill. Furthermore, the \"Explorer Asia\" 81/2016 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 01/2026) & \"Explorer Oceania\" 81/2015 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 12/2025) from Caravel Group were committed to Chinese interests at USD 41 mill enbloc. Note that the \"Sea Marathon\" 81/2015 Qingdao, China (SS/DD 09/2025) was sold in April at USD 18,4 mill. Kobe Shipping have committed the Handysize \"Aries Sakura\" 39/2020 Shin Kurushima, Japan (SS 06/2030, DD 05/2028) to Greek interests at USD 25,5 mill. For reference, the OHBS \"Nord Abidjan\" 38/2020 Minaminippon, Japan (SS 01/2030, DD 02/2028) was sold in April at USD 25,5 mill. In addition, the \"CS Crystal\" 30/2010 Tsuji, China (SS/DD 06/2025) was committed to Korean interests at USD 10 mill, while the \"Vantage Reef\" 29/2010 Nantong, China (SS/DD 06/2025) was sold in April at USD 8,5 mill.",
    "tankers": "Clients of Yasa Tankers have acquired the VLCC \"C. Spirit\" 314/2013 Hyundai, Korea (SS 04/2028, DD 01/2026, Scrubber fitted) from SK Shipping at low USD 67 mill. Moreover, New Shipping committed their \"New Tinos\" 300/2003 Universal, Japan (SS 04/2030, DD passed) to undisclosed interests at USD 37 mill. Remind you that back in May, same owners sold the sister vessel \"New Naxos\" 300/2003 Universal, Japan (SS 01/2027, DD 04/2025) at USD 33 mill. Teekay Corp have committed the Suezmax \"Montreal Spirit\" 150/2006 Universal, Japan (SS/DD 05/2026) to European interests at region USD 30 mill. Note that the two-years-older sister vessel \"Nordic Castor\" 150/2004 Universal, Japan (SS 07/2029, DD 02/2028) was sold in May at USD 23 mill. Teekay Corp have also committed the LR2 \"Limerick Spirit\" 105/2007 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD 02/2027) to Greek interests at USD 27,8 mill. For reference, the two-years-younger Aframax \"P. Sophia\" 105/2009 Hyundai, Korea (SS 09/2029, DD 11/2027) was sold in April at USD 36 mill. The MR2 \"Nord Oceania\" 50/2018 Onomichi, Japan (SS 01/2028, DD 12/2025) of Norden was committed at USD 37 mill. For comparison, the \"Nord Joy\" & \"Nord Jewel\" 49/2018 JMU, Japan (SS 11/2028, DD 12/2026 & SS 01/2028, DD 11/2027) were sold a month ago at USD 37 mill each.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 11,000/14,000 pd. Indonesian and Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 11,000/13,000 pd. South East Asian trips via South America into China were reported at the level of usd 11,000/13,000 pd. Indian trips via South America into China were fixed around usd 12,000/15,000 pd. Indian trips via South Africa into China were reported at the level of usd 13,000/15,000 pd. South African trips into India were fixed around usd 12,000/13,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 200K/300K. Continental trips via North Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via US Gulf were fixed around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Continental trips into China were reported at the level of usd 20,000/22,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Continent were fixed around usd 14,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 400K. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 20,000/22,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 15,000/16,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 500K/600K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 8,000/11,000 pd. Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Arabian Gulf trips into India were reported at the level of usd 12,000 pd. South African trips into China were fixed around usd 14,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 140K. US Gulf trips into West Africa were reported at the level of usd 20,000 pd. US Gulf trips into North Coast South America were fixed around usd 18,000/20,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 10,000/12,000 pd. Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Indian coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 10,000/11,000 pd. Trips from US East Coast into China were fixed around usd 11,000 pd. North Coast South American trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
